; pdp64 assembly language.  One statement to a line; `;` or `//` starts a comment; `name:` defines a label, and the numeric labels
; `1:` are referenced as `1b` (back) and `1f` (forward); `sym = expr` assigns.  Numbers, characters and strings are C's:
; decimal by default, `0x`, `0b` and `0o` when asked for; `'a'`; `"text\n"`.  Operators are C's (`/` is division).  The
; operand modes are those of ISA section 5.  See docs/asm-syntax.md.
;
; The master of the assembly-language grammar (HAND EDITED): the directives of hbnf, and the one include of the parts.  The rules are the parts of spec/grammars.d/ whose
; `; targets:` line names asm (the syntax is 60-asm-syntax.hbnf; the words, registers and system registers are the other parts), listed in load order by
; the generated spec/generated/index-asm.hbnf (tools/grammars_d.py).  A new mnemonic group, a new system register: a new part there (spec/README.md).  as64 and the checks read this file.
language C
prefix none
whitespace ws
include "generated/index-asm.hbnf"
%start asm
